C1@@src/main.zrl@@// The file's contents; empty when it cannot be read.@@// The file's contents; empty when it cannot be read at all.@@C1: a comment-only edit in src/, which changes no behaviour - the canary for the SURVIVED verdict. A harness that reports this as caught cannot report a surviving mutant, which is how every mutation of a whole day looked caught.
C2@@src/lower_zir/expr.zrl@@"logical operator requires bool operands"@@"logical operator requires bool operand types"@@C2: one diagnostic's wording changed, which exactly one located error test pins (tests/error_reporting/ec_bool_logical_int.zrl) - the canary for the caught verdict. A harness that does not report this as caught cannot report a real miscompile either.
C4@@src/main.zrl@@// The file's contents; empty when it cannot be read.@@// The file's contents; empty when it cannot be read at all.@@Control canary for the incremental path: a no-op, so the scenario must report it SURVIVED. Without this, a scenario that fails for an unrelated reason is indistinguishable from a catch.
C5@@src/verify.zrl@@            0xffffffffffffffff as u64@@            0 as u64@@Canary for the interface path: an unknown callee is assumed to tie nothing and store nothing. Both occurrences of that constant are the unknown branch of src/verify.zrl, and the whole-program fixpoint marks its own functions known, so this is reachable only through an interface - the scenario's test 49 rejects the stale-interface compile for exactly this reason.
